From 0abcd2db09d9864cdf1993734527993f245b743b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:05:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] hs_cache: Count fetches of each descriptor over a
 per-descriptor rate

An HSDir queues the whole descriptor for every fetch it answers. During
a flood such as the one in tor#41339, an operator can't tell whether
the fetches concentrate on a few descriptors or spread over many, and
that decides whether any per-descriptor defense could help.

Give each cached descriptor a fetch token bucket, kept when the
descriptor is replaced, with HSDirDescriptorFetchRate (default 5 per
second) and HSDirDescriptorFetchBurst (default 20), and count fetches
that find it empty as tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_fetch_over_rate"}.
Compared with tor_relay_hsdir_get_total{action="success"}, it shows the
shape of a flood: one on a few descriptors moves both, one spread over
many moves only the latter. Nothing is refused, and the counter is
relay-wide, so it says nothing about any one descriptor.

Part of #41339.
